  "body": "Split from #173 (PR #522 added probing for Haas, Mazak and Sinumerik 840D).\n\n**Today:** the Heidenhain post refuses a Probe operation by name.\n\n**Expected:** probing hooks for Heidenhain TNC (ISO/DIN mode). Map the touch, guard, result, tolerance alarm and work-offset write onto the control's documented probing functions, cited from the TNC user's manual (Programming of Measuring/Probing Cycles). Keep the named refusal for anything it can't state exactly.\n\n**Done means:** Heidenhain posts a probe face/edge/bore program with protected positioning, a tolerance check before the offset write and a named alarm on no contact; goldens and per-dialect tests like probe_dialects; no control available here, so tests and golden review only.",
